<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0020">Notation <span data-tag="0020">1.2.3.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set. It follows immediately from the definitions that if there exists a map $u: S \rightarrow \operatorname{Sing}_{\bullet }(Y)$ which exhibits $Y$ as a geometric realization of $S$, then the topological space $Y$ is determined up to homeomorphism and depends functorially on $S$. We will emphasize this dependence by writing $| S |$ to denote a geometric realization of $S$. By virtue of Example <a data-tag="001Z" href="/tag/001Z">1.2.3.2</a>, this is compatible with the convention of Notation <a data-tag="050B" href="/tag/050B">1.2.2.1</a> in the special case where $S = \Delta ^{n}$ is a standard simplex. </p>
</article>
